{
  "run_id": "506bd51d10",
  "final_message": "**Status:** Reproduced\n\n**Expected:** `<template #_duration>` content replaces the child's default slot content, as in Vue 3.5.13, even when the child component sits next to a conditional `<template v-if #name>` in the parent's slots.\n\n**Actual:** The child renders its default fallback for the `_`-prefixed slot. The non-underscore slot (`title`) works. Rendered output: `<div><p>conditional</p><b>title-slot</b><i>default-duration</i></div>`.\n\n**Trigger:** Both conditions are needed.\n- The parent component (`BaseLayout`) receives a `<template v-if=\"...\" #someSlot>` as a slot, which makes its slots dynamic. The `v-if` can be true, and it is also reproduced when it is false.\n- The child (`SubComponent`) inside that parent has a slot whose name starts with `_`.\n\nControls on this revision, using the same harness:\n\n| Variant | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Same page without the `v-if` template | Passes |\n| Static `<template #randomslotname>` with no `v-if` | Passes |\n| `v-if` template, slot renamed to `duration` (no underscore) | Passes |\n\nThe compiled render function for the report's page looks correct. The problem shows up at runtime.\n\n**Run:** `npx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts` (from the repo root). It exits 1 now.\n\n**Passes when:**\n- With the `v-if` sibling template removed, the same spec passes (exit 0).\n- Published `vue@3.5.13` renders `duration-slot` for the same page (run with a script outside the repo, `/tmp/rc/pub.cjs`, which asserts the same thing).\n- Published `3.5.14` and `3.5.17` render the default fallback, so the regression lands in 3.5.14 as reported.\n\n**Likely cause (not traced):** a slot-handling change in 3.5.14 that mishandles `_`-prefixed slot keys when the parent's slots are dynamic.\n\n**Artifacts:** `packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts` (new, the only change in the repo). No production code was changed.\n",
  "run_command": "npx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts",
  "patch": "diff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts b/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..adf867d\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@\n+import { createApp, defineComponent } from '../src'\n+\n+// Slot <template> whose name starts with \"_\" must replace the child's default\n+// slot content, even when the child sits next to a conditional\n+// <template v-if #name> in the parent component's slots.\n+test('#_duration slot template replaces default content next to a conditional sibling slot', () => {\n+  const BaseLayout = defineComponent({\n+    template: `<div><slot name=\"randomslotname\"></slot><slot></slot></div>`,\n+  })\n+  const SubComponent = defineComponent({\n+    template: `\n+      <slot name=\"title\"><i>default-title</i></slot>\n+      <slot name=\"_duration\"><i>default-duration</i></slot>`,\n+  })\n+  const App = defineComponent({\n+    components: { BaseLayout, SubComponent },\n+    data: () => ({ ok: true }),\n+    template: `\n+      <BaseLayout>\n+        <template v-if=\"ok\" #randomslotname><p>conditional</p></template>\n+        <SubComponent>\n+          <template #title><b>title-slot</b></template>\n+          <template #_duration><b>duration-slot</b></template>\n+        </SubComponent>\n+      </BaseLayout>`,\n+  })\n+\n+  const root = document.createElement('div')\n+  createApp(App).mount(root)\n+\n+  expect(root.innerHTML).toContain('title-slot')\n+  expect(root.innerHTML).toContain('duration-slot')\n+  expect(root.innerHTML).not.toContain('default-duration')\n+})\n"
}
